      "html": "<p>Origin: Brazil, Rio Negro.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/rineloricaria_melini_en/",
      "html": "<p>They live in blackwater biotopes in the Rio Negro area.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/rineloricaria_melini_en/",
      "html": "<p>An aquarium for Rineloricaria should have densely planted zones, as well as open areas and some caves.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/rineloricaria_melini_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are omnivores and need both vegetable and animal food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
